# Aventus Astra V3 — research and model decision record

Date: 2026-09-05. Scope: woody/ambrox-led Aventus architecture, deliberately restrained pineapple and blackcurrant. Native local review and primary-source web research only; no external model providers or plugin installation. No claim of exhaustive literature coverage.

## Finding that determines the implementation

Existing `creed_aventus.reference` and `CREED_AVENTUS_OFFICIAL_NOTES_V2` already represent an architecture, not an authenticated formula. The existing dry-wood gate combines several materials and cannot require Ambrox independently. Its 8% fruit ceiling is a broad uncalibrated heuristic, not protection against the user's observed fruit overload. The new opt-in engine component keeps the official contract unchanged and adds a separately labeled mass-design geometry.

The old SUKHUM R1/F2 family uses 800/790 microlitres of 10% ACP and 250 microlitres of 10% AAG. The stock-volume allocation is verified in those files; an exact active-mass or sensory reduction factor cannot be inferred without comparable stock bases and mass records. The new candidate removes ACP and does not use Paradisamide, fruit esters or opaque cassis bases as additional fruit carriers. The new 0.25% AAG allowance is on aromatic-material mass, not raw stock volume.

The requested exact earlier “Astra V3, Layered Whole-Batch Candidate” recipe was not supplied or located. The new file uses the requested title but is an independent design; no fictitious immediate parent or active-equivalence claim is attached. Older formulas remain unchanged.

## Primary-source ledger

| Evidence | What it supports | What it does not establish |
|---|---|---|
| [Creed US Aventus](https://creedboutique.com/products/aventus), accessed 2026-09-05 | Dry-woods family; citrus/blackcurrant head, pineapple/pepper/jasmine heart, birch/patchouli/musk base | Ingredient identities behind accords, percentages, or a measured temporal curve |
| [Creed Aventus collection](https://www.creedfragrance.com/c/fragrances/aventus-collection/), accessed 2026-09-05 | A separately presented architecture including ambergris and woody grounding | Proof that the US note pyramid changed chemically, batch identity, or an Ambrox concentration |
| [DSM-Firmenich Ambrox Super NEO](https://studio.dsm-firmenich.com/product/ambroxr-super-neo-pe-909100) | Manufacturer describes ambery, woody, musky character spanning top through drydown; its page gives VP 0.00219 Pa at 20 C | User bottle's exact grade, a transferable threshold, or Creed's use/dose of this product |
| [IFF Iso E Super](https://www.iff.com/scent/ingredients-compendium/iso-e-super/) | Smooth woody-amber material, useful to the dry-wood scaffold | Equivalence to cedarwood, Ambrox, or a whole perfume |
| [Firmenich Romandolide technical advertorial](https://www.firmenich.com/sites/default/files/uploads/files/ingredients/advertorials/SI_1/magic_inside_romandolide.pdf) | Delicate fruity musk character; relevant cross-facet risk | A numerical pineapple-equivalence factor or sensory outcome in this candidate |
| [DSM-Firmenich Habanolide](https://studio.dsm-firmenich.com/product/habanolider-pe-947303) | Macrocyclic musk with a warm, slightly woody undertone | That 12% is optimal here or that metallic/laundry drift is impossible |
| [Time and Intensity Factors in Identification of Components of Odor Mixtures](https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC2955077/), 2010 human experiment, PMID 20720093 | Component identification changes with adaptation, intensity and mixture suppression | Calibration of any Aventus ratio, universal component-count limits, or OAV as perceived percentage |
| [IFRA Birch wood pyrolysate Standard 114](https://ifrafragrance.org/standards/IFRA_STD_114.pdf) | Distinction between crude prohibited pyrolysate and specified rectified fractions | Permission to ignore the inventory's explicit birch prohibition or lot documentation |
| [IFRA Cade Standard 119](https://ifrafragrance.org/standards/IFRA_STD_119.pdf) | Rectified-grade specification and PAH control; crude material is prohibited | Safety approval of the user's specific bottle or the complete perfume |

These are paraphrased observations, not a reconstructed commercial formula. The two Creed descriptions are kept as distinct observations. No authentic quantitative Creed assay was established in this review.

## Material choices and alternatives

All inventory categories were reviewed. Selection is target-linked, not an ingredient-count or longevity contest. Quantities below refer to the companion candidate, not a proprietary formula.

| Register | Selected hypothesis and reason | Alternatives considered and why not selected here |
|---|---|---|
| Dry-wood volume and grain | Iso E Super plus Virginia cedar: abstract woody space plus a distinct natural cedar facet | Cedramber, Vertofix, Timberol, Koavone, Azarbre, Amberwood F, Kephalis, Cashmeran, Norlimbanol Dextro and Amber Xtreme: different dry/amber/spicy intensity profiles would add variables; sandalwoods Ebanol/Bacdanol/Sandalore/Javanol introduce creamy or sandalwood emphasis; other cedars/vetiver/cypress shift the selected grain |
| Crystalline ambergris-like axis | Current Ambrox Super, protected separately at 16% aromatic mass | More Iso E Super or superambers cannot count as Ambrox. Ambrofix liquid is gone; crystals are a distinct non-executable stock. No chemical/olfactory equivalence is inferred |
| Chypre return | Patchouli plus Evernyl, 7.2% and 0.8% aromatic mass, respectively | Clearwood is a controlled patchouli alternative, not automatic equivalence. Oakmoss absolute adds composition/lot complexity; no need for a generic balsamic/sweet fixative. Guaiacwood carrier remains unresolved; depleted Nagarmotha is excluded |
| Musk | One Habanolide slot, selected after manufacturer evidence highlighted Romandolide's fruit facet | Romandolide remains a separate comparator, not layered into the selected design. Ambrettolide, Exaltolide, Zenolide, ethylene brassylate and Galaxolide offer different body/texture or stock uncertainties. Tonalide, Macrolide and Musk Ketone remain excluded. Habanolide's possible metallic/laundry dominance needs a controlled trial |
| Floral transition | Hedione as transparent jasmine-linked bridge, not a complete natural jasmine reconstruction | Jasmine Sambac stock and jasmone/dihydrojasmone would add a new composition or trace variable; salicylates, muguets, rose, iris and lactonic florals do not solve the specific fruit-to-wood transition as cleanly in this first test |
| Citrus | Bergamot FCF Sicilian primary, Lemon FCF Sicilian secondary at a 9:2 mass relation | Grapefruit, citron/cedrat, mandarin/orange, neroli/petitgrain, methyl pamplemousse, Pamzest, Lemonile and other citrus modifiers are alternatives, not mandatory additions. Avoid sweetness or long-lived fruit substitution |
| Cassis | Trace Blackcurrant Absolute as green/sulfurous tension; natural-composite evidence required | Cassis Base 345B is an opaque base. Dynascone, hexenols and other greens are not blackcurrant-equivalent and could create harshness. Berry/lactone/damascone additions are intentionally absent |
| Pineapple | AAG alone at 0.25% aromatic mass: a bounded green-pineapple marker | ACP is removed from the selected whole-batch design. E2MB, Hexyl Acetate, Paradisamide and other fruit enhancers are not added to make a large “realistic pineapple” object |
| Pepper | Schinus molle EO ideal bridge, with inventory synchronization HOLD | Black pepper, elemi, coriander, ginger, juniper, cardamom and other aromatics cannot silently fill the pink-pepper identity slot |
| Smoke/leather | Trace rectified Cade plus neat Suederal as a conditional functional approximation | Birch tar remains excluded under current inventory instructions. IBQ, Guaiacol, tobacco, styrax and other leather/resin materials have different facets or stock/identity constraints; Suederal alone is not smoke, Cade alone is not leather |

Single-material names can refer to commercial isomer mixtures; they are not assertions of analytical purity. Natural EO/absolute aromatic mass means mass of that natural product, not mass of one molecule. Habanolide replaces Romandolide in this new candidate only; historical architecture and formulas are preserved.

## Quantities, OAV and data limitations

The live inventory SHA-256 at design time is `5da7ecdab4ce9c297f95a61051b38d9183f796c1971dd276546ef15c7856c497`.

Ambrox Super is 25% **w/w**, from 3 g active + 7 g DPG + 0.5 g IPM + 1.5 g ethanol. Thus 0.960 g target active requires 3.840 g stock and brings 2.240 g DPG, 0.160 g IPM and 0.480 g ethanol. No stock density is needed for that mass statement. None of it establishes microlitres. Evernyl is 10% w/w in DEP: 0.048 g active requires 0.480 g stock and brings 0.432 g DEP.

Blackcurrant Absolute 10% DPG, AAG 10%, and Cade 1% DPG have no declared mass/volume basis in the current inventory. Their required stock masses remain null. A historical design note is not used to silently overwrite the inventory. Schinus is already user-confirmed owned in the prior architecture record, but is not synchronized in the live inventory; this is not a request to reconfirm ownership.

The local ODT table has estimates and multiple metadata/numeric entries. Naturals must use `engine/pipeline/natural_absolute_decomposition.py`; no single-molecule ODT is assigned to an EO or absolute here. The manufacturer Ambrox NEO VP and existing local Ambrox proxy have different grade/temperature contexts, so no automatic data-spine rewrite is justified.

For later validated screening: solution OAV requires solution concentration and a matching solution ODT; air OAV requires vapor ppm divided by air ODT ppm (`ODT_ppb / 1000`). Never divide concentrate ppm by an air threshold. No OAV sum is a perceived percentage. Current ODT/OAV values are deliberately null, not zero/subthreshold. A numerical headspace curve, projection range, skin longevity or safety conclusion would be unsupported.

## Integration and scope

The pure module lives in `engine/formulation_intelligence/aventus_woody_geometry.py`; its candidate data are `data/reference/aventus_astra_v3_woody_candidate.json`. `future_modules.iconic_formulas.get_aventus_woody_mass_design()` is an opt-in entry point. The existing official-note model is not replaced. No new pipeline script, provider, optimizer default, inventory record, threshold value or release gate was added or bypassed.

The volumetric formula-release interface cannot execute this incomplete gravimetric plan. The research artefact is a model/ideal candidate, not a released compounding revision. Once stock bases, the matrix and measured volume/density inputs are resolved, prepare a separate executable child card, provide its actual immediate parent where applicable, run active-dose/OAV-per-time checks, and present the full existing formatted analysis. Do not create a nominal-density card merely to obtain a pipeline report.

